        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement US, Israel war on Iran US Developing Trump hails ‘decisive victories’ in Iran but vows more strikes in next few weeks US president tells anxious Americans that the conflict’s core objectives are ‘nearing completion’ 3 -MIN READ 3 -MIN 12 Listen Khushboo Razdan in Washington Published: 9:22am, 2 Apr 2026 Updated: 9:58am, 2 Apr 2026 US President Donald Trump on Wednesday declared the US‑Israel war against Iran had delivered “decisive, overwhelming victories”, even as he signalled that key military objectives were still “nearing completion” and that further strikes could inflict heavy damage on targets in Iran. “Over the next two to three weeks, we are going to bring them back to the stone ages, where they belong. In the meantime, discussions are ongoing,” he said in a televised address to the nation. WATCH: Donald Trump addresses nation WATCH: Donald Trump addresses nation As the highly unpopular conflict has rapidly escalated into a regional and global crisis, Trump appeared to reassure the American public and ask for patience. Advertisement “Our objectives are very simple and clear. We are systematically dismantling the regime’s ability to threaten America or project power outside of their borders,” he said, adding that “the core strategic objectives are nearing completion.” “Armed forces have delivered swift, decisive, overwhelming victories on the battlefield – victories like few people have ever seen before,” Trump said. Advertisement “Never in the history of warfare has an enemy suffered such clear and large-scale losses in a matter of weeks,” he added, claiming that Iran’s navy was “absolutely destroyed” and the air force was in “ruins”. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
